//DNS Privé
Prérequis
    Pihole, un un nom de domaine avec https

Installer stunnel
    sudo apt update && sudo apt install stunnel4 -y
Faire la config
    sudo nano /etc/stunnel/stunnel.conf
    ```
pid = /run/stunnel4/stunnel4.pid

[dns-over-tls]
accept  = 853
connect = 127.0.0.1:53
cert    = /etc/letsencrypt/live/<nom de domaine>/fullchain.pem
key     = /etc/letsencrypt/live/<nom de domaine>/privkey.pem
    ```
        Attention à bien changer <nom de domaine>
Activer
    sudo sed -i 's/ENABLED=0/ENABLED=1/' /etc/default/stunnel4
    sudo systemctl enable stunnel4
    sudo systemctl start stunnel4
    sudo systemctl status stunnel4
